<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tokugawa Yorifusa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1603–1661</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tokugawa Yorifusa (1603–1661) was the eleventh son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> and the founder of the Mito branch of the Tokugawa family, one of the three senior houses (gosanke) entitled to provide a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a>. He received the Mito domain in Hitachi province in 1609 and ruled it until his death, when his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-mitsukuni">Tokugawa Mitsukuni</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tokugawa-yorifusa.jpg" alt="Tokugawa Yorifusa" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tokugawa_Yorihusa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
